# Legal CRM Domain Rules

## Responsibilities

- Encode legal practice management domain knowledge in software
- Ensure workflows match how law firms operate
- Protect ethical and compliance requirements in feature design

## Domain Model Overview

| Entity | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **Client** | Individual or organization receiving legal services |
| **Case/Matter** | Legal matter linked to client; central hub for all related data |
| **Hearing** | Court dates, depositions, mediations |
| **Document** | Contracts, filings, evidence, correspondence |
| **Task** | Deadlines, follow-ups, assignments |
| **Invoice** | Billable work product; line items from time/expenses |
| **Payment** | Client payments against invoices |
| **Expense** | Case-related costs (filing fees, travel) |
| **Note** | Internal case notes (privileged) |
| **Activity** | Timeline of all actions on records |
| **CalendarEvent** | Firm calendar including hearings and meetings |
| **AuditLog** | Compliance trail for sensitive changes |

## Best Practices

- **Case-centric navigation** — everything accessible from case detail
- **Conflict check** before new client/case creation (Phase 3)
- **Statute of limitations** tracking with alerts (Phase 4)
- **Time tracking** in 0.1 hour increments (6-minute billing)
- **Trust accounting** separation (IOLTA) — Phase 5
- **Document versioning** — never overwrite, always version
- **Privilege markers** on notes and documents
- **Activity feed** auto-generated from all CRUD operations

## Legal Workflows

```
Intake → Conflict Check → Open Case → Assign Team
  → Document Management → Task/Deadline Tracking
  → Time Entry → Invoice → Payment → Close Case
```

## Coding Standards

- Case numbers: auto-generated per org `{PREFIX}-{YEAR}-{SEQ}` (configurable)
- Invoice numbers: sequential per org, never reused
- Status transitions validated (can't close case with open invoices)
- Hearing reminders: 24h and 1h before (configurable)
- Document categories: enum aligned with legal practice (Pleading, Contract, Evidence, Correspondence, Filing)

