## Naming Convention

| Domain Term | Code Term | UI Label |
|-------------|-----------|----------|
| Matter | Case | Case / Matter (configurable) |
| Client | Client | Client |
| Hearing | Hearing | Hearing / Court Date |
| Time Entry | TimeEntry | Time Entry (Phase 3) |

## Performance Rules

- Case detail page: load overview first, lazy-load tabs (documents, billing)
- Activity feed: cursor pagination, 20 items per page
- Global search: cases, clients, documents (Phase 2)

## Security Rules

- **Attorney-client privilege**: notes/documents restricted by role
- **Ethical walls**: restrict case access by user assignment (Phase 3)
- **Client portal**: separate auth, limited to own cases/invoices (Phase 4)
- **Export controls**: audit all data exports
- **Retention policies**: configurable per org (Phase 5)

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — Validate case closure
async closeCase(caseId: string, session: Session) {
  const openInvoices = await invoiceRepository.countOpen(caseId);
  if (openInvoices > 0) {
    return { success: false, error: 'Cannot close case with unpaid invoices' };
  }
  return caseRepository.updateStatus(caseId, 'CLOSED', session.organizationId);
}

// ✅ GOOD — Auto activity on mutation
await activityService.log({
  entityType: 'CASE',
  entityId: caseId,
  action: 'STATUS_CHANGED',
  metadata: { from: 'OPEN', to: 'CLOSED' },
  userId: session.userId,
});
```

## Things to Avoid

- Deleting cases with legal hold
- Mixing trust and operating account logic prematurely
- Showing privileged notes to client portal users
- Allowing invoice edits after payment received
- Generic CRM terminology that confuses legal users

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Feature fits legal workflow (case-centric)
- [ ] Status transitions validated
- [ ] Activity logged for audit trail
- [ ] Privilege/access rules respected
- [ ] Legal terminology consistent in UI and code
- [ ] Empty states guide user through legal workflow step
